35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,The reviews show high satisfaction when any department could book the space. Projects argued for comfort or appeal slipped a year or more.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The timetable data is stark. Every room closed for works required paid off-site space for two terms. That is a massive hidden cost.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The tender data confirms my fear. Mechanical plant costs jumped a fifth, while the schedule data shows comfort projects slip a year.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The reserve is empty. We bought kit, wrote it down, but never saved for replacement. The surveys show hazardous material in older blocks, adding months.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The freeze left grounds posts empty, yet technicians still burn hours on manual checks. We are bleeding capacity while pretending the system works.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Benjamin, your schedule data aligns with my findings. Inspection-driven projects stay on track, but comfort-based ones slip. We must prioritize utility over appeal.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, I agree. The booking data shows general rooms are always full, while specialist ones sit idle. We need high utilization to justify the cost.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the empty reserve is a disaster. We are funding new builds with money meant for old repairs. That is a recipe for failure.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, exactly. The market prices have shifted, and our paper figures are obsolete. The hazardous material in older blocks proves that hidden costs always emerge.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, the hazardous material is a symptom. The real failure is that we have no hands to fix it. The technicians are drowning in manual labor.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, the manual labor is a symptom of poor design. If we build spaces that are easy to maintain, we reduce that burden.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, I see your point. But if we choose a space that is widely bookable, we reduce the need for constant, specialized intervention.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, I agree. If we pick a project with a clear inspection rationale, the schedule data suggests it will actually finish on time.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, the empty reserve means we are absorbing those hidden costs now. I need to see if the new plan accounts for that market reality.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, the market is irrelevant if we have no one to operate it. I need a plan that doesn’t require a miracle worker to keep the lights on.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I am ready to see the candidates. We need a plan that is widely useful, on schedule, and easy to maintain.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I am ready. The data points to a general-purpose space that minimizes downtime and maximizes utilization.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am ready. The numbers are clear: avoid mechanical plant and comfort-driven projects. We need a plan that respects the budget and the calendar.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I am ready. We must pick a plan that accounts for the empty reserve and the hidden costs in older blocks.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I am ready. The data is clear: we need a project that does not require a miracle worker to keep the lights on.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
