60,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,The post-occupancy data strongly favors a space that is widely accessible and bookable. Candidate A fits that profile perfectly.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Candidate A is an indoor conversion. It avoids the weather delays and the high-cost mechanical plant issues affecting the other options.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate D is a trap. My tender data shows mechanical plant costs jumped a fifth. We cannot afford that surprise.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Candidate C is a nightmare. The surveys show hazardous material in older blocks, and path work means digging up exactly that. Hidden costs will explode.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Candidate D is a staffing suicide. My data shows technicians already drown in manual checks. Adding complex ventilation maintenance will break the remaining crew.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
