68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, exactly. Candidate A avoids the empty reserve trap. It is a simple conversion, so the market costs stay predictable.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mizuki, Candidate A is the only one that doesn't require a miracle worker. The service desk is simple, and the open layout means no complex systems to babysit.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
